# What the shared em and en dash gate (@cosyte/script-utils) leaves out of its scan of this
# repository: one tracked path per line, anchored at the repository root.

# THE CHANGELOG'S ARCHIVE, read for the em dash alone. Every entry above "Released before this file
# was generated" is written by the release tool from a changeset and is read for both dashes like
# any other file. From that heading down is the frozen archive of releases before the tool, which is
# never hand-edited and holds en dashes in old ranges, so it is read for the em dash in every form
# and an en dash there passes. This is the reading the former repository gate gave the file. A
# heading the file no longer carries is refused, so this cannot outlive its subject.
CHANGELOG.md em-only below ## Released before this file was generated
